IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III.1, Division 3 Entitlement, first half: regs 76.09 to 76.18, then
-- 76.22 and 76.23 (disentitlement, the adaptations of the Act, the reduction of benefits, no double counting, the waiting
-- period and the transition). The weeks arithmetic of regs 76.19 to 76.21 is in module er4-part3-1-weeks.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified against the
-- official text". No section GIVEN: every rule has its own GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATIONS. A claimant who is entitled to provincial benefits (QPIP is the instance the Regulations name in reg
-- 76.08) is disentitled to maternity and parental benefits under ss 22 and 23 of the Act (76.09(1)) unless, at their
-- request, the Commission has found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent (76.09(2)); then ss 22 and 23
-- benefits are reduced by the provincial amount week by week (76.16, 76.17). For any other benefit under Part I or the
-- Fishing Regulations the bar is week by week (76.09(3)). The Commission's finding is a BOOLEAN input and is never guessed.
-- A reading rule that the text states ("adapted", "read as including") is encoded as the rule that gives the adapted
-- result, and cites the reg that adapts it.

§ `Regulation 76.09 -- disentitlement`

§§ `Regulation 76.09(2) -- the Commission's determination on the claimant's request`

-- src:1216 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if, at the request of the claimant, it is determined by the Commission that the amount of provincial benefits the claimant is entitled to receive under the provincial plan is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of benefits that they are entitled to receive under section 22 or 23 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(2) (src:1216)
GIVEN `the claimant has asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has determined that the amount of provincial benefits the claimant is entitled to receive is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of benefits they are entitled to receive under section 22 or 23 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.09(2) subsection (1) does not apply` IF
        `the claimant has asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent`
    AND `the Commission has determined that the amount of provincial benefits the claimant is entitled to receive is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of benefits they are entitled to receive under section 22 or 23 of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 76.09(1) -- benefits under section 22 or 23`

-- Whole claim: unlike (3), (1) does not speak of a week (fork F18).
-- src:1215 | 76.09 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act if they are entitled to receive provincial benefits under a provincial plan.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(1) (src:1215)
GIVEN `the claimant is entitled to receive provincial benefits under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.09(1) the claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act` IF
        `the claimant is entitled to receive provincial benefits under a provincial plan`
    AND (NOT `subsection (2) applies`)

§§ `Regulation 76.09(3) -- any other week of benefits under Part I or the Fishing Regulations`

-- src:1217 | (3) Every claimant who has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits under a provincial plan in respect of any week is disentitled to be paid benefits in respect of that same week under
-- src:1218 | (a) Part I of the Act, other than benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act; or
-- src:1219 | (b) the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(3) (src:1217-1219)
DECLARE `er4 Benefits claimed by a claimant with provincial benefits` IS ONE OF
    `er4 benefits under section 22 of the Act`
    `er4 benefits under section 23 of the Act`
    `er4 other benefits under Part I of the Act`
    `er4 benefits under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`
    `er4 benefits of another kind`

-- "Received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of any week" bars the same
-- week of Part I benefits (other than ss 22 and 23) and of Fishing Regulations benefits. For ss 22 and 23 subsection (1)
-- governs, not this one, so (3) alone says FALSE of them; for a benefit of another kind (for instance Part VII.1 benefits,
-- which reg 76.36 covers) it says nothing: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(3) (src:1217-1219)
GIVEN benefits IS A `er4 Benefits claimed by a claimant with provincial benefits`
      `the claimant has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefits
    WHEN `er4 other benefits under Part I of the Act` THEN JUST `the claimant has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of the week`
    WHEN `er4 benefits under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` THEN JUST `the claimant has received, or has applied for and is entitled to receive, provincial benefits in respect of the week`
    WHEN `er4 benefits of another kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 76.09(4) -- for greater certainty: moving province`

-- Whether the claimant, after applying, ceases to reside in the province where the plan was established makes no
-- difference, so it is not an input (asserted in the tests): what brings the claimant within (1) to (3) is having applied
-- for and being entitled to receive the provincial benefits.
-- src:1220 | (4) For greater certainty, subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of a claimant who has applied for and is entitled to receive provincial benefits under a provincial plan even if the claimant, after making that application, ceases to reside in the province where that plan was established.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(4) (src:1220)
GIVEN `the claimant has applied for provincial benefits under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is entitled to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.09(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the claimant whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province where the plan was established` IF
        `the claimant has applied for provincial benefits under a provincial plan`
    AND `the claimant is entitled to receive them`

§§ `Regulation 76.09(5) -- the other person caring for the same child`

-- "Subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person": read as bringing the other person under the same bars,
-- as though entitled to the provincial benefits themselves (fork F19). The other person is an insured person (a) or a
-- self-employed person (b), to whom reg 76.36(1) to (3) apply.
-- src:1221 | (5) For greater certainty, if two persons are caring for the same child or children and one of them is a claimant referred to in subsection (4),
-- src:1222 | (a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person if that other person is an insured person; and
-- src:1223 | (b) subsections 76.36(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person if that other person is a self-employed person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(5)(a) (src:1221-1222)
GIVEN `two persons are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them is a claimant referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.09(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` IF
        `two persons are caring for the same child or children`
    AND `one of them is a claimant referred to in subsection (4)`
    AND `the other person is an insured person`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(5)(b) (src:1221-1223)
GIVEN `two persons are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them is a claimant referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.09(5)(b) subsections 76.36(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` IF
        `two persons are caring for the same child or children`
    AND `one of them is a claimant referred to in subsection (4)`
    AND `the other person is a self-employed person`

§ `Regulation 76.11 -- insured participant`

-- The definition in Act s 58 (out of range: section 58 of the Act, piece ei2) is adapted to include an insured person
-- who requests assistance under employment benefits and, when requesting it, is an unemployed person who has a
-- benefit period established under a provincial plan, or has had that benefit period end within the previous 60 months,
-- and who would have been entitled to special benefits under s 22 or 23 had they not been entitled to provincial benefits.
-- src:1227 | 76.11 The definition insured participant in section 58 of the Act is adapted to include an insured person who requests assistance under employment benefits and, when requesting the assistance, is an unemployed person who has a benefit period established under a provincial plan or has had that benefit period end within the previous 60 months and who would have been entitled to receive special benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act had they not been entitled to provincial benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.11 (src:1227)
GIVEN `the person is an insured participant under section 58 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an insured person who requests assistance under employment benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `when requesting the assistance the person is an unemployed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a benefit period established under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person's benefit period under a provincial plan ended, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the person requests the assistance` IS A DATE
      `the person would have been entitled to receive special benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act had they not been entitled to provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` IF
        `the person is an insured participant under section 58 of the Act`
    OR  (    `the person is an insured person who requests assistance under employment benefits`
         AND `when requesting the assistance the person is an unemployed person`
         AND (    `the person has a benefit period established under a provincial plan`
              OR  (CONSIDER `the day the person's benefit period under a provincial plan ended, if it has`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                   WHEN JUST ended THEN `add months` ended 60 AT LEAST `the day the person requests the assistance`))
         AND `the person would have been entitled to receive special benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act had they not been entitled to provincial benefits`)

§ `Regulations 76.1 and 76.12 -- repealed`

-- src:1224 | 76.1 [Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 3]
-- src:1228 | 76.12 [Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 5]
-- (no operative text: the sections are blank in this text)

§ `Regulation 76.13 -- a week not counted to extend the qualifying period`

-- src:1231 | 76.13 The reference to “a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits” in subsection 8(5) of the Act shall be read as including a week for which the person was paid provincial benefits within the meaning of this Part or Part III.2.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.13 (src:1231)
GIVEN `the person was in receipt of benefits in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was paid provincial benefits in the week within the meaning of Part III.1 or Part III.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.13 the week is a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits, for subsection 8(5) of the Act` IF
        `the person was in receipt of benefits in the week`
    OR  `the person was paid provincial benefits in the week within the meaning of Part III.1 or Part III.2`

§ `Regulations 76.14 and 76.15 -- extension of the benefit period`

-- (a) Provincial benefits paid for the reasons in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act (pregnancy, and the care of a
-- new-born or adopted child) are included in "benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a)
-- and (b)" in subsection 10(13) of the Act.
-- src:1234 | 76.14 For the purpose of extending a claimant’s benefit period under subsection 10(13) of the Act,
-- src:1235 | (a) a reference in that subsection to benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act is considered to include a reference to provincial benefits paid for the same reasons; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.14(a) (src:1234-1235)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the benefits were paid under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits were provincial benefits paid for the same reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.14(a) the benefits count as benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act` IF
        (    reason EQUALS `pregnancy`
         OR  reason EQUALS `caring for a new-born or adopted child`)
    AND (    `the benefits were paid under the Act`
         OR  `the benefits were provincial benefits paid for the same reason`)

-- (b) The benefit period is extended so that benefits paid for a reason in paragraphs 12(3)(c) to (f) may be paid up
-- to the applicable maximum number of weeks for that reason, not "that maximum total number of weeks" of s 10(13).
-- The two maxima are inputs (out of range: Act ss 10(13) and 12(3), piece ei1).
-- src:1236 | (b) the reference in that subsection to “the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid up to that maximum total number of weeks” shall be read as a reference to “the benefit period is extended so that those benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(c) to (f) may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks established for those reasons”.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.14(b) (src:1236)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason` IS A NUMBER
      `that maximum total number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` THEN `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason`
    WHEN `care or support of a family member` THEN `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason`
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill child` THEN `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason`
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill adult` THEN `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason`
    OTHERWISE `that maximum total number of weeks`

-- src:1237 | 76.15 If the child or children of a claimant who has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act, the claimant’s benefit period is considered to be extended under subsection 10(12) of the Act by the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.15 (src:1237)
GIVEN `the claimant has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.15 the number of weeks by which the benefit period is considered to be extended under subsection 10(12) of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the claimant has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits`
    THEN JUST `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulations 76.16 and 76.17 -- reduction of benefits`

-- src:1240 | 76.16 The benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act to a claimant in respect of any week in respect of which the claimant has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits shall be reduced as provided by section 76.17.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.16 (src:1240)
GIVEN `the claimant has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.16 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week are to be reduced` IF
    `the claimant has received or is entitled to receive provincial benefits in respect of the week`

-- The amount deducted is the provincial benefit for the same week, "in addition to any deductions referred to in
-- section 19 and subsections 22(5) and 23(3.5) of the Act" (out of range: piece ei1). If that deduction exceeds what
-- is left to pay, the text does not say what happens: NOTHING, not zero.
-- src:1241 | 76.17 An amount equal to the amount of the provincial benefits that a claimant has received or is entitled to receive in respect of any week under a provincial plan shall be deducted from the amount of benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act to the claimant in respect of that same week, in addition to any deductions referred to in section 19 and subsections 22(5) and 23(3.5) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.17 (src:1241)
GIVEN `the benefits payable for the week after the deductions referred to in section 19 and subsections 22(5) and 23(3.5) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the provincial benefits the claimant has received or is entitled to receive in respect of the same week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.17 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` MEANS
    IF `the benefits payable for the week after the deductions referred to in section 19 and subsections 22(5) and 23(3.5) of the Act` AT LEAST `the provincial benefits the claimant has received or is entitled to receive in respect of the same week`
    THEN JUST (`the benefits payable for the week after the deductions referred to in section 19 and subsections 22(5) and 23(3.5) of the Act` MINUS `the provincial benefits the claimant has received or is entitled to receive in respect of the same week`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 76.18 -- no double counting of weeks`

-- src:1244 | 76.18 If a week of provincial benefits has been taken into account for the purpose of any of sections 76.11 to 76.14 or 76.19, a week of benefits paid under section 22 or 23 of the Act shall not be taken into account for that same purpose.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.18 (src:1244)
GIVEN `a week of provincial benefits has been taken into account for that purpose under any of sections 76.11 to 76.14 or 76.19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.18 a week of benefits paid under section 22 or 23 of the Act may be taken into account for that same purpose` IF
    NOT `a week of provincial benefits has been taken into account for that purpose under any of sections 76.11 to 76.14 or 76.19`

§ `Regulation 76.22 -- waiving of the waiting period`

-- Paragraph 40(6)(b) (out of range: reg 40, piece er3) is read as "... were payable to the claimant ... as sick leave pay
-- or provincial benefits were paid to the claimant". This rule gives the adapted condition of that paragraph.
-- src:1274 | 76.22 The reference in paragraph 40(6)(b) to “allowances, payments or other moneys are payable to the claimant by the claimant’s employer or former employer as sick leave pay” shall be read as a reference to “allowances, payments or other moneys were payable to the claimant by the claimant’s employer or former employer as sick leave pay or provincial benefits were paid to the claimant”.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.22 (src:1274)
GIVEN `allowances, payments or other moneys were payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provincial benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.22 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` IF
        `allowances, payments or other moneys were payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay`
    OR  `provincial benefits were paid to the claimant`

§ `Regulation 76.23 -- coming into force of the provincial plan: transition`

-- "The day on which this Part comes into force" is not in the text of the Regulations in this range; it is an input
-- (reg 76.23, NOTES.md Dates). A claim for a birth or placement before that day stays under the Act (a); so does a claim
-- for a birth or placement for which the claimant had before that day been paid at least one week under s 22 or 23 (b).
-- src:1277 | 76.23 For greater certainty,
-- src:1278 | (a) if a birth or a placement for the purpose of adoption takes place before the day on which this Part comes into force, the Act applies in respect of any claim for benefits made in respect of that birth or placement; and
-- src:1279 | (b) if a claimant has, before the day on which this Part comes into force, been paid one week or more of benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act in respect of a birth or a placement for the purpose of adoption, the Act continues to apply in respect of any claim relating to that birth or placement.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.23(a) (src:1277-1278)
GIVEN `the day on which the birth or the placement for the purpose of adoption takes place` IS A DATE
      `the day on which this Part comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.23(a) the Act applies in respect of a claim for benefits made in respect of the birth or placement` IF
    `the day on which the birth or the placement for the purpose of adoption takes place` LESS THAN `the day on which this Part comes into force`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.23(b) (src:1277-1279)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act paid to the claimant before the day on which this Part comes into force in respect of the birth or placement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.23(b) the Act continues to apply in respect of any claim relating to the birth or placement` IF
    `the weeks of benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act paid to the claimant before the day on which this Part comes into force in respect of the birth or placement` AT LEAST 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.23 (src:1277-1279)
GIVEN `the day on which the birth or the placement for the purpose of adoption takes place` IS A DATE
      `the day on which this Part comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the weeks of benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act paid to the claimant before the day on which this Part comes into force in respect of the birth or placement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.23 the Act applies to the claim as it did before this Part` IF
        `reg 76.23(a) the Act applies in respect of a claim for benefits made in respect of the birth or placement`
            `the day on which the birth or the placement for the purpose of adoption takes place` `the day on which this Part comes into force`
    OR  `reg 76.23(b) the Act continues to apply in respect of any claim relating to the birth or placement`
            `the weeks of benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act paid to the claimant before the day on which this Part comes into force in respect of the birth or placement`
